:[{"text":"கொண்ட","lemma":"கொள்","gloss":"having"}],"gloss":"having"},{"surface":"உருகெழு","parts":[{"text":"உரு","lemma":"உரு","gloss":"awe"},{"text":"கெழு","lemma":"கெழு","gloss":"possessing"}],"gloss":"possessing awe"},{"surface":"சிறப்பின்","parts":[{"text":"சிறப்பு","lemma":"சிறப்பு","gloss":"excellence"},{"text":"இன்","lemma":"இன்","gloss":"of"}],"gloss":"of excellence"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"மாலை","parts":[{"text":"மாலை","lemma":"மாலை","gloss":"garlanded"}],"gloss":"garlanded"},{"surface":"வெண்குடை","parts":[{"text":"வெண்குடை","lemma":"வெண்குடை","gloss":"white umbrella"}],"gloss":"white umbrella","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"ஒக்குமால்","parts":[{"text":"ஒக்கும்","lemma":"ஒப்பு","gloss":"resembles"},{"text":"ஆல்","lemma":"ஆல்","gloss":"indeed"}],"gloss":"resembles indeed"},{"surface":"எனவே","parts":[{"text":"எனவே","lemma":"எனவே","gloss":"therefore"}],"gloss":"therefore"}]}],"literal":"Like the lamp of a fishing boat in the middle of the ocean / In the vast sky where stars twinkle / Having seen the full moon standing at the zenith / Like a peacock of the forest roosting place that reached the edge of the desert path / The female dancer with few bangles and I, greatly hastening / Did we not worship many times indeed? In the seashore grove / Scooping up backwater salt and supplying it to the hilly country / Removing the sinking of the spoked wheel of the cart / Like the strong, enduring bull is our king / The Chola king with a victorious sounding drum and a sharp sword / Whose garlanded white umbrella of awe-inspiring excellence / That is held to shield from the sun, it resembles indeed, saying so!","translation":"In the vast sky where stars twinkle like the lamps of fishing boats in the middle of the ocean, we saw the full moon shining at its zenith. Like a peacock from its forest roosting place reaching the edge of the desert path, the female dancer wearing a few bangles and I hastened to worship it many times. For we said, 'This resembles the garlanded white umbrella of our king, the Chola ruler of victorious drums and sharp swords, which is held to shield from the sun with awe-inspiring excellence—just like the strong, enduring bull that pulls out a heavy cart when its spoked wheels sink into the mud as it carries backwater salt to the hilly country!'","modern":"கடலின் நடுவே மீன்பிடிப் படகின் விளக்கைப் போல, விண்மீன்கள் ஒளிரும் பரந்த வானத்தின் உச்சியில் நின்ற முழு நிலவைக் கண்டு, காட்டில் வாழும் மயில் பாலைநிலத்தின் எல்லையை அடைந்தது போல, சில வளையல்களை அணிந்த விறலியும் நானும் மிக விரைந்து பலமுறை தொழுதோம். கடற்கரைக் கானலில் உப்பங்கழி உப்பை ஏற்றி மலைநாட்டிற்குச் செல்லும்போது, சேற்றில் சிக்கிய வண்டியின் ஆரக்கால்களைக் கொண்ட சக்கரத்தை மேலே தூக்கி இழுத்துச் செல்லும் வலிமைமிக்க எருதைப் போன்றவன் எங்கள் அரசன். வெற்றி முரசும் கூர்மையான வாளும் கொண்ட சோழ மன்னனின் வெயிலை மறைக்கும் பெருமை மிக்க மாலை அணிந்த வெண்கொற்றக் குடையைப் போல இந்த நிலவு இருக்கிறது என்று கூறி நாங்கள் அதனைத் தொழுதோம்.","explanation":"The poet Uṟaiyūr Maruttuvaṉ Tāmōtaraṉār praises the Chola king Kurāppaḷḷit Tuñciya Perun Tirumā Vaḷavaṉ in this poem. The poet describes how he and his female dancer (viṟali) saw the full moon in the night sky and mistook it for the king's glorious white umbrella, prompting them to worship it. This comparison of the full moon to the royal umbrella is a classic trope of praise (kuṭai maṅkalam). The poet uses a vivid simile of a strong bull pulling a salt-laden cart out of the mud to illustrate the king's protective strength and the relief he brings to his subjects. The peacock simile highlights the grace and eagerness of the dancers traveling through difficult terrains to reach their patron.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.6],[0.6,0.8],[0.8,1.4],[1.4,1.8],[1.8,2.9],[2.9,3.0],[3.0,3.3],[3.3,3.6],[3.6,4.1],[4.1,4.8],[5.33,5.39],[5.39,5.7],[5.7,6.6],[6.6,6.8],[6.8,7.6],[7.6,8.0],[8.0,8.8],[8.8,9.1],[9.1,9.4],[9.4,9.6],[9.6,10.0],[10.0,11.5],[11.5,11.6],[11.6,12.1],[12.1,12.9],[13.1,13.8],[13.8,14.2],[14.2,14.56